  The article says the 79 mm rain was recorded in the Billur dam catchment area, but the headline and slide headline present it as rain at the Billur dam itself, which is a slight shift in location.
  The reel_script and caption say the water level (40.34 ft) rose ('உயர்ந்தது'/'ஆனது') and attribute the increase to rain; the article only says the level became 40.34 ft and does not describe it as a rise.
  The reel_script's ambiguous phrase 'மக்களின் குடிநீர் தேவைக்காக' adds a purpose ('for drinking water needs') not stated in the article, which says only that 7.18 crore litres was supplied to people.
  The caption says the 40.34 ft water level belongs to 'சிறுவாணி அணை' (Siruvani dam), while the article does not explicitly name which dam the water level refers to; the reel_script also assigns it to the Siruvani dam.
  The reel_script and caption say the rain 'started in the first week' as forecast by meteorologists, which matches the article, but the reel_script states 'தொடங்கியுள்ளது' as if completed; this is a minor wording issue rather than a factual error.
